        "contact": {
          "name": "Hunter Van Lear"
        },
        "description": "Provides access to Stephen King books, short stories, and villains. Retrieve information by ID.",
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "Production server",
            "url": "https://stephen-king-api.onrender.com"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Stephen King API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "x-documentation": "https://stephen-king-api.onrender.com/",
        "tagline": "Look up Stephen King's books, short stories, and villains by ID",
        "homepage": "https://stephen-king-api.onrender.com",
        "docs_url": "https://stephen-king-api.onrender.com/docs",
        "license_short": "Free, open-source community project (no formal licence stated).",
        "license_md": "- Described by the maintainer as \"free, open-source\"; no formal licence text is published alongside the API.\n- Created and maintained by Hunter Van Lear ([hvanlear](https://github.com/hvanlear) on GitHub) — see the [Stephen-King-API repository](https://github.com/hvanlear/Stephen-King-API).\n- Stephen King's works and characters remain the intellectual property of their respective rights holders; treat returned data as catalogue metadata for fan/educational use.\n- No specific attribution requirement is stated, but a courtesy credit to the project is appropriate.",
        "about_md": "The [Stephen King API](https://stephen-king-api.onrender.com) is a small, community-run REST service that catalogues Stephen King's literary universe. It is built and hosted by [Hunter Van Lear](https://github.com/hvanlear) on Render, and is also indexed on [Free Public APIs](https://freepublicapis.com/stephen-king-api).\n\nWhat you get from the API:\n\n- Books — id, `Year`, `Title`, `handle`, `Publisher`, `ISBN`, `Pages`, `Notes`, related `villains`, `created_at`.\n- Short stories — id, `title`, `type`, `handle`, `originallyPublishedIn`, `collectedIn`, `notes`, `year`, related `villains`, `created_at`.\n- Villains — id, `name`, `gender`, `status`, `types_id`, `notes`, related `books` and `shorts`, `created_at`.\n- List endpoints support optional pagination via `page` and `limit` query parameters (used together; `limit` capped at 100).\n\nThe API is read-only (GET requests only), returns JSON, and requires no authentication. CORS is enabled, so browser clients can call it directly. As a free service hosted on Render's free tier, cold-start latency on first request is common; no formal rate limits are published.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "book": "A Stephen King book entry with bibliographic fields (title, year, publisher, ISBN, pages) and linked villains; available at `/api/books` and `/api/books/{id}`.",
          "short": "A Stephen King short story with title, type, year, original publication, collection it appears in, and linked villains; available at `/api/shorts` and `/api/short/{id}`.",
          "villain": "An antagonist or monster from King's works with name, gender, status, notes, and back-references to the books and shorts they appear in; available at `/api/villains` and `/api/villain/{id}`."
        },
